# Flag 1 – Unauthorized Policy Handler Execution

## Invariant
Only authorized and intended policy handler functions must execute
during request processing.

## Telemetry
No runtime instrumentation was possible because the binary exposes
no hooks for policy handler attestation or execution verification.
The assessment evaluates the absence of such telemetry.

## Observation
Observed. The system assumes correct policy handler execution but
does not verify it. An unintended or substituted handler could
execute without detection as long as functional output remains valid.

## Security Impact
Unauthorized policy execution can silently bypass access control
logic, undermining authorization guarantees in security-critical
systems.

## Limitations
This assessment does not exploit the binary; conclusions are based
on absence of enforcement and telemetry rather than live attacks.
